  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "An unprecedented deluge, the heaviest in three decades, drove a surge on the Euphrates that overwhelmed engineered defenses. The river's force reshaped the landscape of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa, invading homes, farms, and schools. As storage systems were pushed to their limits, an earthen bridge gave way, severing a vital link. In the wake of the destruction, rescue craft were put into service for evacuations, while young lives were tragically lost to the waters.",
