      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The crisis was framed by an upstream partner in crisis management, Turkey, who committed to flow reduction after pressure yielded a reduction in upstream discharges. This accord was a key piece of the response architecture, aimed at lessening the force that had critically overfilled reservoirs. The head of state then surveyed the crafted response in the affected areas, observing the aftermath where emergency watercraft had been mobilized.",
